  "notes": [
    "1 to 3 Infantry Brigades: 1 or 2 Line (or Light) Infantry regiments of 1-4 battalions, plus Regimental Artillery.",
    "0 to 1 Cavalry Brigade (1 per 2 Infantry Brigades): up to 2 Chasseur à Cheval regiments.",
    "Divisional Artillery: up to 1 Foot and 1 Horse battery (1 per 8 infantry battalions), attached to any brigade.",
    "0 to 1 Italian Guard Brigade: up to 1 regiment each of Guard Infantry, Royal Velite Infantry and Guard Conscript Infantry, plus up to 2 Guard Dragoon regiments and Guard artillery.",
    "Reserve Artillery: up to 2 Heavy Foot Artillery batteries (1 per 10 infantry battalions), attached to any brigade.",
    "Allies: an Italian army can take 25% allies from any one allied list."
  ]
